WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.334
-Guys, it is summer,

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.734
and I'm always looking for
a good book to read, okay?

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.634
A good beach read, okay?

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.601
Now, in the past,
we've done contests on the show.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.133
We'd pick a few books and then
vote on which one to read.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:11.167
But this year,
we're not doing that.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.300
-What?

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.400
-We're doing things
a little different.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.901
I made a decision this year.
-What?

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.334
-I just picked a book.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.367
I chose --
I'm doing a book club.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.968
This is --
We're all doing the book club.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.868
Yeah. Yeah. Everyone.
Roots, everybody.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.334
-You got it?
-Mandatory book club.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.968
-Oh!
-Yeah.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.334
That's the way we do it here.
This year, it's mandatory.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.667
-We have to read it?
-You have to read it.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.300
-Aw!
-Yeah.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.868
-Can somebody read it to me?
-No, this one's fantastic.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.167
I picked it out.
It's a good one.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.200
I love it.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.501
It involves --
It's a love story.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:37.567
-Love it.
-You love love?

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.801
-Yeah.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:42.634
-About two kids that --
They love each other.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.667
It's in the '90s.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.100
They create
a video game together.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.667
-Oh!

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.801
-And then it just gets --
Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:52.801
It is called "Tomorrow,
and Tomorrow, and Tomorrow"

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.434
by Gabrielle Zevin, everybody.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.534
This is the book.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.634
This is it.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.534
It's officially
the very first book

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.167
in our brand-new
Fallon Book Club.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.267
-Ooh.
-Look at that.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.834
We have a sticker.
Look at the sticker.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.601
Can we zoom in?

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:09.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, yeah!

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.734
-Oh, man! FBC!

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.267
-That's as much as we
could zoom in?

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.701
-FBC!

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.801
-It feels like the camera zoomed
in a little bit, then stopped.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:17.868
-We can't afford that.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:21.100
-Yeah! Look at that.
That's tight.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.567
But look --
Just holding it looks cool.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.767
-Oh, nice!
-What's up man?

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:31.234
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.234
[ Rhythmic clapping ]

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:41.167
Okay. I can't wait. This is --
-Beach!

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.734
-It's got everything you want
in this thing.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.934
This is the summer read,
the Fallon Book Club.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.133
This is the jam right here.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:50.200
It says here, "A dazzling
and intricately imagined novel

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.033
that imagines the nature of
identity, failure,

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.434
the redemptive possibilities
in play, and, above all,

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.834
our need to connect,
to be loved, and to love.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.400
Yes, it is a love story,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.434
but it is not one
you have read before."

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.300
-Ooh!
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.868
-So, here's how this works.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.567
-Wow.
-That was good, right?

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:08.868
-Yeah.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.667
-I'm going to be reading this
over the next few weeks,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.901
and if you want to
read along with me,

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.567
pick up a copy
wherever books are sold

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.000
or go to your local library.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.834
I'll be posting
my updates on my socials

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.033
about where I'm at in the book,
what I think of it.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.000
And then we're going to have
the author, Gabrielle Zevin,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.601
on the show
to talk about the book.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.767
It's a book club.
-Hey!

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.000
-Some people
don't know about book clubs.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.033
-No, never.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.534
-I ain't gonna join
no book club.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.634
-What?

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.334
-I don't want to join
no book club.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.367
-Well, here, try this book.
-What the heck?

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.968
-It's called "Tomorrow,
and Tomorrow, and Tomorrow."

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.767
-I like this book.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.167
I'm going to be in
more book clubs.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.167
-I'm going to be in
way more...

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:45.133
[ Inhales deeply ]
...book clubs.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.934
Is it part of the FBC?

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:49.167
-Oh, you're in the FBC!

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.100
Fallon Book Club.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.434
-2022.
-2022.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.567
[ Imitates air horn blowing ]

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.167
[ Air horn blows ]
Thank you, yeah.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.934
-Vuvuzela!

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.367
-Vuvuzela!
What does that mean?

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.000
But, anyways, to start,
to kick things off,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.067
tonight,
everyone in our studio audience

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.267
will be going home
with their very own copy of

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.501
"Tomorrow, and Tomorrow,
and Tomorrow."

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:14.934
That's what I'm saying.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.267
It's a Fallon Book Club!

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.033
[ Imitates air horn blowing ]

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.067
[ Air horn blows ]

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:24.734
Happy reading, everybody!

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:29.634
♪♪

